- # Security Controls

- Never weaken authentication, authorization, or token handling. Client uses memory + sessionStorage for tokens; no localStorage.
- Preserve security headers (HSTS, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, CSP).
- File uploads must enforce MIME validation, size limits, malicious pattern scanning, and (if configured) virus scanning.
- Sanitize inputs and validate requests server-side; use parameterized queries and avoid leaking sensitive details in errors.
- Mask PII in logs. Detect and redact emails, phone, SSN, credit card, and JWTs.
- Respect CORS restrictions and HTTPS enforcement.
- Do not commit secrets. Use environment variables and existing config mechanisms.
- Do not add new `.env` / `.env.example` keys unless a new integration or deployment surface requires it — see [env-vars-minimal.mdc](./env-vars-minimal.mdc).
